hadiths[44]{hadithnumber,text}:
"80","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any one of you performs ablution, let him rinse his nose, and when he uses stones (for istinja), let him use an odd number."
"81","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When he sits between her four limbs, then makes an effort (has intercourse), then ghusl becomes obligatory upon him."" Mutar (the narrator) has added: even if there is no ejaculation."
"82","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When he sits between her four limbs and then exerts himself (has intercourse), then ghusl (ritual bath) becomes obligatory upon him."
"83","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a dog puts its mouth in the vessel of any one of you, then wash it seven times, and one of those times with earth."
"84","Muhammad bin Ziyad al-Qurashi narrated, that our master Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, saw some people performing ablution from a vessel, so he said: Perform ablution thoroughly, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: “Woe to the heels (left) dry (during ablution) from the fire of Hell.”"
"85","Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw some people performing ablution from a vessel, so he mentioned something similar to that."
"86","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Gold locusts rained down upon Ayub (peace be upon him), so he began to gather them. Allah revealed to him: 'Have I not given you abundance?' He replied: 'Yes, my Lord! But I cannot do without Your bounty.'"
"87","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Musa (peace be upon him) was extremely modest and would cover his body, and due to his modesty, no part of his body could be seen. Some individuals from Bani Israel caused him harm and said: The reason he covers his body to such an extent is only because there is some defect in his body, or he has leprosy, or his private parts are enlarged, or he has some other illness. So, he began to bathe and placed his clothes on a stone, then the stone ran away with his clothes. He (Musa, peace be upon him) also ran after it. The Bani Israel saw him (naked) and found him to be the best of men. Thus, Allah made his innocence clear from the accusation. That is why Allah the Exalted said: O you who believe! Do not be like those who caused harm to Musa (peace be upon him), and Allah declared him innocent of what they alleged."
"88","Abu Zar’ah narrated: I entered a house in the company of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), which was being built in Madinah for Sa’id or Marwan. When Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) performed ablution, he washed his hands up to the armpits and his feet up to the knees. I said to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): What is this? He replied: This is the utmost limit of purification (the final extent of attaining purity). The narrator stated: He saw a painter making a picture in the house, so he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Who can be more unjust than the one who tries to create like My creation? Let them create a particle, let them create a grain.”"
"89","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went to the toilet, so I brought a vessel of water to him. He performed istinja (cleaning) with it, then rubbed both his hands on the ground and then washed them. Then I brought another vessel, and he performed ablution (wudu) with it."
"90","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the strap of the shoe of any one of you breaks, he should not walk wearing the other shoe until he repairs it, and when a dog puts its mouth in the vessel of any one of you, he should wash it seven times."
"91","Abu Zurayn narrated: I saw Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, in Iraq, striking his hand on his forehead, and he was saying: O people of Iraq! Do you say that I would attribute a lie to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, so that you may have comfort and the sin would be upon me? I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""When a dog puts its mouth in the vessel of any one of you, he should wash it seven times, and when the strap of his shoe breaks, he should not walk in the other until he repairs it."
"92","Abu Idris Khawlani narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to this."
"93","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: When the verse of tayammum was revealed, I did not know how I should perform it. So I went to the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to present myself to him, but I did not find him. It was said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has gone outside. I knew the path where I could find him, so I followed behind him. I think he sensed my need, so he stood up, then struck both his hands on the earth, wiped his face and hands, and did not add anything to that. I returned and did not ask him (about the method of tayammum)."
"94","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): Some Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! We stay in this desert for three or four months, among us are women in postnatal bleeding and menstruation, and also strangers, and we do not find water, (what should we do?) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Use earth (and perform tayammum)."
"95","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any of you performs ablution, he should not shake his hands, for they are the fans of Satan."
"96","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Wipe over the leather socks and the head covering, for indeed it is the truth."
"97","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The five prayers and one Jumu'ah to the next Jumu'ah are an expiation for the sins committed in between them, as long as major sins are avoided."
"98","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه narrated from the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم, he صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""None of you should intend to pray without purification."
"99","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever goes to a soothsayer and affirms what he says, or has intercourse with a menstruating woman, or has intercourse with a woman from her back, then such a person is dissociated from the Shari'ah revealed upon Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"100","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution should clean his nose, and whoever uses stones for istinja should use an odd number of stones."
"101","Sayyida Rabi’ bint Mu’awwidh bin ‘Afra’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and a large vessel of water was placed before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) washed the limbs of ablution three times each, and wiped his head twice."
"102","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqil bin Abi Talib narrated: I went to Sayyida Rubayyi’ bint Mu’awwidh bin ‘Afra’ (may Allah be pleased with her), so she said: Who are you? I said: I am Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqil. She asked: Who is your mother? I said: Raytah bint Ali or so-and-so bint Ali. She said: Nephew! Welcome. I said: I have come to you to ask about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). She said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to come to us, and he performed ablution from this vessel, or a vessel like it, and it is about the size of a mug (approximately ten chittank). He washed both hands, then rinsed his mouth, cleaned his nose, and washed his face three times, then washed his hands three times each, then wiped his head twice, wiped the inner and outer parts of his ears, then washed his feet three times each. Then she said: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) came to me and asked me about this hadith, so I informed him, and he said: People only accept washing, while we find wiping in the Book of Allah, that is, regarding the feet."
"103","It is narrated from Qaboos bin Mukhaariq that Husayn bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them) was in the lap of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he urinated on him. Umm al-Fadl (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me your garment so that I may wash it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umm al-Fadl! The urine of a girl should be washed, and the urine of a boy should be sprinkled with water."
"104","Lubabah bint al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took Husayn bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) and seated him in his lap, and he urinated on him. So I said: O Messenger of Allah! Give me your lower garment so that I may wash it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The urine of a girl is washed, and water is sprinkled over the urine of a boy."
"105","Umm Ayman (Barakah bint Tha'labah) رضي الله عنها narrated, the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Hand me the mat."" She said: ""I am in a state of menstruation."" So the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Your menstruation is not in your hand."
"106","Lady Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I was beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and when he would prostrate, my garment would touch his garment while I was menstruating."
"107","Ubaid bin Umair narrated, Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to instruct women that when they performed ghusl (ritual bath) after janabah, they should untie their hair. When this reached Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: He has put them in great hardship; why does he not just order them to shave their heads? I used to perform ghusl with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) from a single vessel, and I would only pour three handfuls of water."
"108","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while she was menstruating."
"109","The noble wife of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her), narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""Perform ablution (wudu) after (eating or drinking) whatever has been touched by fire (cooked on fire)."
"110","Sayyiduna Ibn Abi Saeed Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from his paternal aunt that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ate the meat of a goat's foreleg, then performed prayer and did not perform ablution."
"111","Lady Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: We did not consider the white, muddy, or yellowish discharge (after becoming pure from menstruation) to be of any significance."
"112","Nu’man bin Kharbuz narrated: I heard Umm Sabi’ah Juhaniyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrate: Sometimes, while performing ablution from the same vessel, my hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would touch each other."
"113","The sister of Sayyiduna ‘Ukkasha bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyida Umm Qais bint Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with her), came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with her nursing infant son and placed him in your lap. He urinated on you, so you took water in your hands and poured it over that (spot), and did not add anything further to it."
"114","Ibrahim Nakha'i, may Allah have mercy on him, stated that he (the student of Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him) liked to use the miswak after witr and before the two rak'ahs."
"115","It is narrated from Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah that he used to use the miswak before the two rak'ahs after Witr."
"116","Syedna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by two graves and said: ""They are being punished, and they are not being punished for a major sin. One of them used to spread gossip, while the other did not protect himself from his urine."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for a fresh date-palm branch, split it into two parts, and placed one on each grave, and said: ""It is hoped that their punishment will be lessened as long as these do not dry out."
"117","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by two graves and said: ""They are being punished, and they are not being punished for a major sin."" Then he said: ""Yes, one of them..."" The narrator mentioned the rest of the hadith similar to the previous narration."
"118","Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated similarly from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"119","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a garden in Makkah or Madinah, and he heard the voices of two people who were being punished in their graves. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are being punished, but they are not being punished for a major sin: one of them used to spread gossip, while the other did not protect himself from urine."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took a fresh date palm branch, split it into two, and placed one piece on each grave. He was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Why did you do this?"" He replied: ""Perhaps their punishment will be lessened as long as these do not dry out."
"120","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he came out from the toilet. Then food was presented to him and it was said: Will you not perform ablution? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why? If I am going to pray, I will perform ablution."
"121","Amr has narrated the same with this chain of transmission."
"122","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""If you would not neglect, I would have commanded you to use the miswak at the time of every prayer."
"123","Narrated by Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), his maternal aunt's goat died, so she threw it outside. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why did you not benefit from its skin?"
